1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
We'll be right back.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
We'll be right back.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,820
I'm just so thankful for each and every one of you.

4
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:06,520
Our church really is a special place to be, and it's not because of the building we meet

5
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:06,720
in.

6
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:12,140
It's not because of anything other than the people that have built the culture around our

7
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:15,480
idea of what Jesus has called us to as a church.

8
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:17,340
And so I'm thankful for all of you.

9
00:01:17,340 --> 00:01:22,220
This morning, we're wrapping up a little two-week series that we started last week, just on kind

10
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:24,540
of the vision for our church in 2026.

11
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:29,740
And last week, I introduced this idea that I really want 2026 to be a time where those

12
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:34,400
of us who would consider ourselves followers of Jesus, that we would take steps towards

13
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,460
maturity in our faith.

14
00:01:36,460 --> 00:01:43,260
Two years ago, or in 2025, we had this focus of being a church that is welcome to those

15
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:44,640
who aren't yet following Jesus.

16
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:49,040
And what did it look like for us to make room for people who are struggling with, wrestling

17
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:51,760
with their faith and pursuing faith in Jesus?

18
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:56,440
And I want to hold those two things in tension because I always want to be a church where people

19
00:01:56,440 --> 00:02:01,540
who are outside of the faith can come and can explore faith and can ask hard questions.

20
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:08,420
But at the same time, we as a church can lose our witness to the world if we actually aren't

21
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:10,080
obeying the principles of God's kingdom.

22
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:14,740
If we're gathering together as believers under the name of Jesus and we don't look anything

23
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:19,320
like Jesus, then our witness to the watching world diminishes.

24
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:23,960
And so if we're going to be a church that has influence, has kingdom impact in the world,

25
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:28,040
we have to actually understand what maturity looks like in the kingdom.

26
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:33,260
And so today, I really want to get more practical on what I think maturing faith looks like in

27
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:37,840
the kingdom of God, especially for those of us who are embracing King Jesus in our Western

28
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:39,660
culture in 2026.

29
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:41,280
Sound like a plan?

30
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:45,460
All right, I'm a little more congested than normal, so I'm going to try and fight through

31
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:49,320
that and you guys just work with me.

32
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:49,760
Sound good?

33
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:52,400
I asked you that twice, didn't I?

34
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,340
Just pray.

35
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:53,920
Let's pray.

36
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:57,740
Father, Son, and Holy Spirit.

37
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:06,200
We are grateful for another opportunity to gather together with the saints to cast our

38
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:14,240
mind on you, the lamb who was slain, who is sitting at the right hand of the Father, ruling

39
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:14,940
and reigning.

40
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:22,160
God, it is not just those of us gathered in this room, but there are hundreds of millions

41
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:30,120
of people gathered all around the world seeking to cast their eye on you, the ruler and reiner

42
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:31,280
of all creation.

43
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:36,520
God, that is going to become totally apparent to everyone one day, but until that day comes,

44
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:41,960
may we be a manifestation of what it looks like for you to rule and reign in our lives as

45
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:43,400
individuals and a community.

46
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:50,680
God, so much of our culture is individualized and the kingdom is not an individual thing that

47
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:51,200
we embrace.

48
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:52,840
It is a family that we join.

49
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:59,820
May we be a family who is committed to your kingdom values for your glory, for our good,

50
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:00,820
and for the good of our neighbors.

51
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:02,820
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

52
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:03,720
Amen.

53
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:10,060
Put a few words on the screen here and let me know if you see anything that connects these

54
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:10,420
words.

55
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:15,860
Old news, bittersweet, jumbo shrimp.

56
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:22,140
That's the heartiest amen I've gotten from my father while preaching a sermon.

57
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:26,600
Freezer burn, deafening silence, unbiased opinion.

58
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:27,620
Anybody see?

59
00:04:27,620 --> 00:04:30,720
We've got some oxymorons in the room.

60
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:37,800
Apparent contradictions, terms that we use together, but upon further investigation are at odds with

61
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:38,240
one another.

62
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:43,380
They're phrases that are so normal to our vocabulary and our vernacular that we don't even realize

63
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:46,980
or think about the fact that they contradict one another.

64
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:52,980
And this is a common human experience to not notice contradictions that are familiar to

65
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:53,280
us.

66
00:04:53,280 --> 00:05:00,100
It's a common occurrence from my perspective, pastorally, for many Christians when it comes

67
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:03,400
to the way that we apply the kingdom of God.

68
00:05:04,860 --> 00:05:11,580
Later in our text, we're actually going to see a Greek word for foolishness, and it's actually

69
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:14,940
where we get the word moron, right?

70
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:20,780
It's like there can be this way that we embrace the kingdom, but we embrace it in a contradictory

71
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:21,240
way.

72
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:27,780
We embrace a kingdom of God in a culture of this world, and we blend the two things.

73
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:33,100
And it's a common experience, and honestly, it's impossible to avoid.

74
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:38,200
Every individual person receives the message of the gospel in a particular culture, whether

75
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:43,580
you're here in America in 2026 or our brothers and sisters in house churches in China, they

76
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:47,040
all receive the gospel within a cultural context.

77
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:53,020
Every church exists within a particular culture, and if we are not careful, it will be really

78
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:59,000
easy for us to embrace the message of Jesus without seeing the ways the values of Jesus

79
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:03,000
contradict the values of our larger cultural context.

80
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:09,960
We can become walking oxymorons, and oftentimes we don't even realize we're doing it because

81
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:12,940
the culture that we live in is the water that we swim in.

82
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:14,520
It is the air that we breathe.

83
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:19,840
And so we don't even realize in some ways the way that the values of the kingdom of God come

84
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:24,240
in opposition to the values of our culture of the day.

85
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,500
I love how N.T. Wright puts it.

86
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:25,820
He says,

87
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:31,180
Christians often simply reflect the values and behaviors of their surrounding culture.

88
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:36,280
As any experienced missionary will confirm, when a tribe or ethnic group becomes Christian,

89
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:39,160
the people rarely get the whole package at once.

90
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:44,980
More often than not, Christianity simply becomes an add-on to their existing worldview.

91
00:06:44,980 --> 00:06:51,580
This can result in a confused semi-Christian worldview, or in the worst cases, syncretism,

92
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:57,020
where we just use Christian language to talk about just our cultural values.

93
00:06:57,020 --> 00:07:02,740
He says it can take years or even a generation for their faith to transform.

94
00:07:02,740 --> 00:07:04,760
And this has been my personal experience.

95
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:10,140
I received the gospel of Jesus in an American context, and it's taken me 15 years to begin

96
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:15,980
to see some areas and some ways in which the gospel of Jesus actually confronts my American

97
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:17,040
culture.

98
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:21,980
And I think maturity in the kingdom of God is realizing where the values of the kingdom

99
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:26,340
of God and the values of the culture that we live in come in opposition to one another.

100
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:32,040
And if we are truly embracing Jesus as king, saying these values that my culture builds up,

101
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:35,160
these values that my culture says that I need to champion and chase,

102
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:39,800
I'm actually going to lay them aside for the values of the kingdom of God, the crucified Savior

103
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:43,160
who saved me and who has given me abundant and everlasting life.

104
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:45,060
I'm actually going to go with what he says.

105
00:07:45,060 --> 00:07:53,940
And so maturity looks like us shedding some of our values that, and not all Western values

106
00:07:53,940 --> 00:07:56,300
come up against the kingdom of God, right?

107
00:07:56,300 --> 00:08:01,120
Like there's some beautiful things in our culture that reflect God's image and God's value.

108
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:05,080
There are beautiful things in our culture that people who don't embrace Jesus actually embrace,

109
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:08,640
and whether they call it Jesus values or not, they are Jesus values.

110
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:12,460
And so it's not that everything about being American is anti-Christian.

111
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:18,520
It's that we, as maturing followers of Jesus, we have to be able to distinguish where kingdom

112
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:22,480
values come in opposition to worldly values.

113
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:25,820
And this is the problem that we see in the church at Corinth.

114
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:29,520
We're going to open our Bibles to 1 Corinthians chapter 1 here in just a second.

115
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:33,780
And this is the problem that the Corinth church embraced.

116
00:08:33,780 --> 00:08:37,540
They are a three- to five-year-old church who embraced the values of the kingdom of God,

117
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:42,140
but did not let the values of the kingdom of God challenge their cultural values.

118
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:46,320
They were embracing a kingdom gospel in a Corinthian way.

119
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:53,260
And I think these problems map really well onto the church in America today, individual churches

120
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:55,100
and the church as a whole.

121
00:08:55,100 --> 00:09:02,940
We've embraced the gospel of Jesus in many ways in an American way more than a kingdom way.

122
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:08,280
Corinth was a port city with a very diverse group of people living there, lots of money,

123
00:09:08,380 --> 00:09:11,740
but the money was shared by a small class at the top of the social ladder.

124
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:15,660
They were obsessed with Greek philosophy and wisdom.

125
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:18,420
It was a high value of the Corinthian culture.

126
00:09:18,420 --> 00:09:20,120
Morality was not.

127
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:27,960
Most people living in Corinth had a deep desire to climb the social or economic ladder, no matter

128
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:28,700
the cost.

129
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:32,960
Does that sound familiar at all?

130
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:35,160
Nothing new under the sun.

131
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:37,560
The Corinthian problem is the American problem.

132
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:39,500
Our modern Western culture isn't much different.

133
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:42,400
Our cultural values are built on success.

134
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:44,860
We want to look like we're successful.

135
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:50,340
We want to achieve success doing whatever we can to climb the social or economic ladder.

136
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:59,100
See, the primary issue with this is Christ's definition of his kingdom people in Matthew chapter

137
00:09:59,100 --> 00:09:59,460
five.

138
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:01,600
Let's read it really quick just to set the stage.

139
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:06,100
Matthew chapter five, starting in verse three, Jesus, when he's defining what the people of

140
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:10,040
his kingdom look like, he said, blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom

141
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:10,460
of heaven.

142
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:12,640
Blessed are those who mourn, for they will be comforted.

143
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:14,780
Blessed are the meek, for they will inherit the earth.

144
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:18,940
Blessed are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness, for they will be filled.

145
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:21,680
Blessed are the merciful, for they will be shown mercy.

146
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:24,400
Blessed are the pure in heart, for they will see God.

147
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:27,080
Blessed are the peacemakers, for they will be called children of God.

148
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:33,260
Blessed are those who are persecuted because of righteousness, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.

149
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:39,240
Blessed are you when people insult you, persecute you, and falsely say all kinds of evil against

150
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:40,640
you because of my name.

151
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:45,520
Rejoice and be glad, because great is your reward in heaven.

152
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:50,520
For in the same way, they persecuted the prophets who were before you.

153
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:55,540
Many of us in the room, we'd read these red letters and we'd give a hearty yes and amen,

154
00:10:55,540 --> 00:11:00,300
but if we look at the direction of our lives, we're obsessed with them looking nothing like this.

155
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:03,380
I love how one pastor puts it.

156
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:09,440
He says, the Corinthian church was allowing their culture and worldview to dominate the

157
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:11,220
way they interacted with the gospel.

158
00:11:11,220 --> 00:11:16,640
And often I think that this is the maturity issue in the American church, that we're allowing

159
00:11:16,640 --> 00:11:22,000
our Western culture to dominate the way that we receive and interact with the gospel rather

160
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,480
than the other way around.

161
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:29,860
Jesus doesn't say, my kingdom people are the powerful, successful, influential ones, the

162
00:11:29,860 --> 00:11:34,080
ones good at climbing the social ladder, the ones good at winning cultural status, the ones

163
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:39,400
who retire at 55 and buy the beach property, the ones whose kids get sports scholarships.

164
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:41,460
It's not what he says.

165
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:45,800
He says, blessed are the meek, blessed are the poor in spirit.

166
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:50,160
This is a challenge to us, right?

167
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:51,820
It's the water we swim in.

168
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:54,020
Our culture is just, it is what it is.

169
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:59,400
It's where we exist and we have to see, we have to have eyes to see where the kingdom of

170
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:03,180
God comes in contradiction with the kingdom of this world.

171
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:08,920
Paul's challenge for the Corinthian church and ultimately for us is that we identify where

172
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:12,380
the values of the kingdom of God contradict the values of our culture.

173
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:13,860
And like I said, it's not all of them.

174
00:12:13,860 --> 00:12:17,560
It's not like every value that our culture has is bad.

175
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:21,440
There's a lot of good values, but we have to identify where the values of our culture

176
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:23,220
come against the values of the kingdom of God.

177
00:12:23,220 --> 00:12:29,500
We've got to examine our lives to see where we are embracing a semi-Christian worldview,

178
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:33,860
where we've blended the culture of this world with the culture of the kingdom of God.

179
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:35,240
All of us do it.

180
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:39,640
This message is extremely challenging for me because I've been a follower of Jesus for 20

181
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:44,900
plus years and I've seen all over my life a blending, a semi-Christian worldview.

182
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:50,620
I'm so American in so many ways and that's not all bad, but in some ways it comes in contradiction

183
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:51,260
to the kingdom.

184
00:12:51,260 --> 00:12:58,060
And if I don't examine my life and allow King Jesus to confront some of my values that are

185
00:12:58,060 --> 00:13:02,560
actually in opposition to his kingdom, then I will always kind of live this oxymoronic

186
00:13:02,560 --> 00:13:02,960
life.

187
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:12,020
And if we are going to be a counter witness to the world around us, we can't be this hypocritical

188
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:14,900
semi-Christian life.

189
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:20,080
We have to be all in and that takes time, but we've got to be committed to it.

190
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:24,200
So we've got to identify, examine, and then ultimately redefine what our values are based

191
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:28,040
on the kingdom of God, even when they come against our broader culture.

192
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:33,020
That's what I want to do with the rest of our time, spend time identifying some of the values

193
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:38,580
that are in opposition, examining our lives for where we might be embracing the semi-Christian

194
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:42,160
worldview and then redefine our values based on God's kingdom.

195
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:44,040
Sound like a good roadmap for the rest of our time?

196
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:45,460
All right, good.

197
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:45,980
Let's do it.

198
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:52,960
First Corinthians chapter one, verse 18, Paul says, for the message of the cross is foolishness

199
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:57,300
to those who are perishing, but to us who are being saved, it is the power of God.

200
00:13:57,300 --> 00:13:59,160
Skip down to verse 22.

201
00:13:59,160 --> 00:14:07,960
He says, Jews demand signs and Greeks look for wisdom, but we preach Christ crucified, a stumbling

202
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:10,660
block to the Jews and foolishness to the Gentiles.

203
00:14:10,660 --> 00:14:17,920
But to those whom God has called both Jews and Greek, Christ is the power of God and the wisdom

204
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:18,760
of God.

205
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:26,260
The church in Corinth was a blend of religious Jews and secular Gentiles, but both groups had

206
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:32,820
been heavily influenced by their Corinthian values of climbing the social or economic ladder.

207
00:14:32,820 --> 00:14:37,880
The first critique Paul has is he says, Jews demand signs.

208
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:43,740
And we see this all over the religious people's interactions with Jesus.

209
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:47,240
They're constantly asking Jesus to do more.

210
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:52,240
Dance for us, Jesus, is the phrase that I would put in the mouth of the Pharisees.

211
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:57,800
They constantly want to see him prove himself with miraculous signs and with power.

212
00:14:57,800 --> 00:15:02,020
The religious Jews expected God to show up and overthrow Rome.

213
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:06,760
They wanted a Messiah in the image of the world around them, one who would dominate their enemies

214
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:14,260
with strength and immediately thrust them as religious people into a position of power and influence.

215
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:19,860
And many of us with religious backgrounds and a culture obsessed with success still have this

216
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:20,880
perspective today.

217
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:23,360
We demand signs of God.

218
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:28,180
We have this underlying assumption that following Jesus will result in us having a successful and

219
00:15:28,180 --> 00:15:29,080
influential life.

220
00:15:29,080 --> 00:15:33,020
We expect God to answer our prayers because we are the faithful ones.

221
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:38,720
We expect for him to show up and do miraculous signs in our life so that his name will be glorified.

222
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:40,880
But my question is, what is our ultimate motivation?

223
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:43,800
Is it so that his name will be glorified?

224
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:49,400
Or is it so that we can climb the social and economic ladder of success?

225
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:54,800
We expect that our churches are going to be influential and powerful in our culture because

226
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:57,760
success in our culture looks like power and influence.

227
00:15:57,760 --> 00:16:05,460
And when faith, listen to this, when faithfulness to Jesus doesn't lead to influence and power,

228
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:08,220
we cut corners in order to produce success for ourselves.

229
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:15,920
And the thing about the kingdom of God is Jesus never promises that we will have earthly

230
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:17,500
success and influence.

231
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:19,980
He actually says that you're going to be persecuted for my name.

232
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:26,440
And so we come with these cultural values of success and influence and we say, we're following

233
00:16:26,440 --> 00:16:26,760
Jesus.

234
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:27,860
We're faithful to Jesus.

235
00:16:27,860 --> 00:16:29,200
That means we're going to have influence.

236
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,420
We're going to be successful.

237
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:32,620
And I'm just not so sure that that happens that way.

238
00:16:32,620 --> 00:16:39,920
And then we look, I just, I see it all over these churches that like build their churches

239
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:42,600
based on effective business principles.

240
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:46,180
Market, they bring in marketing firms.

241
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:50,040
I'm just like, man, I don't know.

242
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:56,660
I don't know that that's the kingdom of God as much as it is the semi-Christian worldview

243
00:16:56,660 --> 00:17:01,600
where we're taking the gospel of Jesus in our culture and trying to produce success, trying

244
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:04,580
to climb up the social and economic ladder.

245
00:17:04,580 --> 00:17:08,600
And I just think, I want to remind us that maturity means faithfulness to Jesus at all

246
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:08,920
costs.

247
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:15,660
And we've got to get comfortable with being at the bottom of the ladder if that's what

248
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:17,320
it takes to be faithful to Jesus.

249
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:21,480
And I'm not saying that faithfulness to Jesus doesn't mean that sometimes we'll have some

250
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:22,200
earthly success.

251
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:23,300
That's not what I'm saying.

252
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:29,820
But we've just got to get, we've got to identify where the values of the culture of our day come

253
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:32,120
against the values of the kingdom of God.

254
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:37,840
Earthly success, influence, and power was never a promised outcome of the gospel of the kingdom.

255
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:42,380
And it reflects more on the values of our culture than the values of the kingdom.

256
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:46,860
We need to take a step back and identify the values, where the values of our culture

257
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:50,920
have impacted or even dominated the way that we receive the message of Jesus.

258
00:17:51,060 --> 00:17:53,040
The Jews, the religious, they looked for signs.

259
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:53,940
They wanted power.

260
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:57,400
They wanted God to show up and conquer their enemies now, today.

261
00:17:57,400 --> 00:18:00,660
And if you don't do it my way, on my terms, then I'm not following you.

262
00:18:00,660 --> 00:18:04,980
It says the Greeks looked for wisdom.

263
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:06,380
It's interesting here.

264
00:18:06,380 --> 00:18:08,280
Paul rarely uses this term Greek.

265
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:09,700
He typically uses Gentile.

266
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:14,200
But I think he uses the word Greek intentionally to focus on the fact that the Corinthians were

267
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:15,820
obsessed with Greek philosophy.

268
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:24,040
This was their cultural value was we actually achieved this level of enlightenment and spiritual

269
00:18:24,040 --> 00:18:27,540
like awakening based on our Greek philosophy.

270
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:30,220
The more that we know, the more enlightened that we become.

271
00:18:30,220 --> 00:18:34,340
And it was this way of climbing up this ladder of success.

272
00:18:34,340 --> 00:18:36,380
So he doesn't use the word Gentile.

273
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:39,880
He uses the word Greek to confront their culture and infatuated with Greek philosophy.

274
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:46,040
Many Gentiles in the Corinthian church had accepted the message, but were treating it like some

275
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:51,680
secular philosophy that made them more enlightened, that allowed them to climb up some social ladder,

276
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:53,360
and they held it with arrogance.

277
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:59,440
It was another status game inherited from their culture and not from the gospel of Jesus.

278
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:05,760
And again, many of us, myself included, often still do something resembling this today.

279
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:10,420
We embrace the wisdom of the Scriptures and blend it with the wisdom of our culture to create

280
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:14,980
a semi-Christian worldview that allows us to look down on others as less enlightened and

281
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:15,900
spiritual than we are.

282
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:21,980
And both groups were allowing their cultural values to dominate the way that they interact

283
00:19:21,980 --> 00:19:23,000
with the gospel message.

284
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:27,020
And Paul's first desire for them is that they would identify it.

285
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:28,560
He's just calling it out.

286
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:30,400
Like, look around the culture.

287
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:35,060
The religious Jews in your culture and the secular Greeks in your culture, they both want

288
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:36,360
power and influence.

289
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:39,000
They want wisdom and power.

290
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,640
But we preach Christ crucified.

291
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:46,060
A message that looks foolish to those who are obsessed with power.

292
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:49,180
A stumbling block to those who are obsessed with power.

293
00:19:49,180 --> 00:19:53,040
And it looks foolish to those who are obsessed with wisdom.

294
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:57,820
So first, we've got to identify.

295
00:19:57,820 --> 00:19:58,140
So first, we've got to identify.

296
00:19:58,140 --> 00:20:00,720
And second, we have to examine.

297
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:07,820
We've got to examine where our culture comes in contradiction with the culture of Jesus.

298
00:20:07,820 --> 00:20:09,980
In verse 22, Jews demand signs.

299
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:11,080
Greek looks for wisdom.

300
00:20:11,220 --> 00:20:16,000
But we preach Christ crucified, a stumbling block to the Jews, foolishness to the Gentiles.

301
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:21,160
But to those whom God has called, both Jews and Greeks, all are welcome at the table of Jesus.

302
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:26,600
It's not divided on ethnic boundaries.

303
00:20:26,740 --> 00:20:28,740
All are welcome to the kingdom.

304
00:20:28,740 --> 00:20:36,080
But in order to come to the kingdom, you have to see that Christ is the power of God and the wisdom of God.

305
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:40,420
Paul's rebuke of the Corinthians is focused on Christ crucified.

306
00:20:40,420 --> 00:20:47,320
And I want to point out here that this is not the only angle that you can take when preaching the gospel.

307
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:55,080
We often talk about the cross a lot when we talk about the gospel, but there are plenty of other angles that you could use when talking about the gospel.

308
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:59,480
The empty tomb of the resurrection, the ascension to the right hand of the Father.

309
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:04,760
There are some victorious, powerful images of the gospel that Paul could have used here.

310
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:12,080
But he chooses to use the most shameful, the most weak image of the gospel of Jesus.

311
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:15,520
Because these people need to be rebuked about their obsession with winning.

312
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:18,600
Their obsession with power and influence.

313
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:23,000
And he's doing something very pastoral here.

314
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:26,460
He's telling the church what they need to hear, even though it's hard.

315
00:21:26,460 --> 00:21:30,960
I love, Mursa and I spent some time last year studying the book of Revelation.

316
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:33,620
And there's seven letters to the seven churches.

317
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:39,220
And each one has kind of different challenges and encouragements and rebukes.

318
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:46,260
There's actually two churches in the letters in Revelation that don't receive any rebuke from the apostle John.

319
00:21:46,260 --> 00:21:51,520
And what's interesting to me is you study the two churches that don't receive any rebuke.

320
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:55,380
My assumption is not that they are a perfect church because we know that those do not exist.

321
00:21:56,020 --> 00:21:59,880
But both of those churches were experiencing heavy persecution.

322
00:21:59,880 --> 00:22:03,100
They were being persecuted for being Christians.

323
00:22:03,100 --> 00:22:10,340
And so the apostle John doesn't come alongside these people who are beaten down and broken and dying for their faith and say, you need to clean yourself up.

324
00:22:10,340 --> 00:22:12,100
He just encourages the heck out of them.

325
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:15,160
He reminds them that Jesus was raised, that Jesus ascended.

326
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:19,220
He reminds them that Jesus is sitting on the throne and they don't need to be afraid.

327
00:22:19,220 --> 00:22:23,000
He encourages those who are discouraged.

328
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:33,300
But to a culture that has blended their culture of success and worldly power, he says, you need to focus on Christ crucified.

329
00:22:33,300 --> 00:22:42,380
The image of Christ crucified is the exact opposite of the cultural values of Corinth and the exact opposite of our values of Western culture today.

330
00:22:42,620 --> 00:22:45,060
Crucifixion was shameful for both Jews and Gentiles.

331
00:22:45,060 --> 00:22:47,220
I wouldn't talk about it in polite society.

332
00:22:47,220 --> 00:22:52,660
It was a symbol that would represent the opposite of their cultural values, weakness and foolishness.

333
00:22:52,660 --> 00:23:00,180
But Paul says in the upside down kingdom, Christ crucified is actually the source of true power and true wisdom.

334
00:23:00,180 --> 00:23:03,600
And so he's confronting them.

335
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:06,000
He's saying, examine what you're doing.

336
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:09,800
Examine the message that you've received versus the way that you've received it.

337
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:15,480
You've received a message of a Messiah who was crucified, shamefully.

338
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:25,280
This is the message you've received and you've received it in such a way where you're using it to try and climb the economic and social ladder of status and power and success.

339
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:30,380
Let's examine how these two things might be contradictory to one another.

340
00:23:31,540 --> 00:23:36,360
It says the Christ crucified is the power of God.

341
00:23:36,360 --> 00:23:42,180
Sacrificial love of enemy is actually where true power is found.

342
00:23:42,180 --> 00:23:46,560
It looks like losing, but in the end, it leads to life.

343
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:50,460
Jesus says in his famous sermon on the mountain, he says,

344
00:23:50,520 --> 00:23:57,600
It looks like foolishness to the world around us.

345
00:23:57,600 --> 00:24:01,560
Our world tells us that if somebody comes against you, you come against them harder.

346
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:03,940
If somebody gossips about you, you slander about them.

347
00:24:03,940 --> 00:24:11,180
If somebody does something to you, you do something to them because it's all about a game where we have to push others down to get higher up the ladder.

348
00:24:11,820 --> 00:24:16,900
And Paul says the power of God is found on Jesus Christ crucified.

349
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:22,120
Sacrificial love of not just your neighbor, but also your enemy.

350
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:26,700
Culture says that if someone threatens your safety, you fight back and you win at all costs.

351
00:24:26,700 --> 00:24:33,640
The kingdom says lay down your life for your enemy and trust in the abundant God who owns the cattle on a thousand hills.

352
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:35,480
He has everything in his hand.

353
00:24:35,580 --> 00:24:41,080
If we believe that he is ruling and reigning, then we do not have to achieve success on our own.

354
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:47,780
We do not have to cut corners in kingdom faithfulness in order to produce our own success or victory.

355
00:24:47,780 --> 00:24:49,400
We can trust him.

356
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:50,600
We can love our enemy.

357
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:59,200
It sounds crazy to those of us steeped in American culture, but I will just ask us one question this morning.

358
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:01,080
Actually, I'm going to end up asking you a lot of questions.

359
00:25:01,080 --> 00:25:03,040
I don't know why I always put that in my notes.

360
00:25:03,040 --> 00:25:05,160
I have one question right now in this moment for you.

361
00:25:05,580 --> 00:25:09,320
And that is how well is our cultural value really working?

362
00:25:09,320 --> 00:25:18,320
How well is this rat race to climb the ladder of social economic power and influence really working for us?

363
00:25:18,320 --> 00:25:23,720
Individuals are running this rat race of success until everyone is run into the ground.

364
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:27,020
Exhausted, anxious, disappointed.

365
00:25:27,020 --> 00:25:28,560
No one really wins.

366
00:25:28,560 --> 00:25:33,420
Our nation is building more and more weapons and engaging in more and more wars around the world.

367
00:25:33,520 --> 00:25:36,860
Is that actually leading us to the peace and safety that we are longing for?

368
00:25:36,860 --> 00:25:39,900
The power of God.

369
00:25:39,900 --> 00:25:47,440
Is people who embrace the value of the kingdom of God actually living the values of the kingdom of God?

370
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:58,420
And the beautiful thing about living in a culture that has some countercultural values to the kingdom is that when we are faithful to kingdom values, it's more obvious and apparent.

371
00:25:58,420 --> 00:26:00,720
It becomes the light of the world.

372
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:02,980
It becomes the salt of the earth.

373
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:11,120
But only if we release our cultural values and embrace the values of the kingdom.

374
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:15,980
He says, not only is Christ crucified, the power of God, it is the wisdom of God.

375
00:26:15,980 --> 00:26:19,520
This spiritual feeling of enlightenment that the Corinthians were longing for.

376
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:26,420
This internal sense of they have a relationship with the divine that they were longing for.

377
00:26:26,420 --> 00:26:29,760
It's found in the person who is hanging on the cross.

378
00:26:29,760 --> 00:26:35,440
The love and affirmation that you and I are looking for is found in the person on the cross.

379
00:26:35,500 --> 00:26:38,020
When we were his enemies, Christ died for us.

380
00:26:38,020 --> 00:26:40,120
This is the wisdom of God.

381
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:44,620
The creator of the universe loves you because you were created in his image.

382
00:26:44,620 --> 00:26:46,820
You do not have to do anything to earn it.

383
00:26:46,820 --> 00:26:49,840
You simply need to receive it on the cross.

384
00:26:49,840 --> 00:27:00,900
The thing that the Corinthians were looking for, this enlightenment, this spiritual power that they were looking for, is actually found in Jesus who loved them even when they were his enemies.

385
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:04,220
This is the wisdom of God.

386
00:27:04,220 --> 00:27:08,860
The thing I love about this is the Jews and the Greeks, they had the right instincts.

387
00:27:08,860 --> 00:27:12,420
The Corinthian believers, they were looking for the right things.

388
00:27:12,420 --> 00:27:13,880
They wanted to see God's power.

389
00:27:13,880 --> 00:27:15,360
They wanted to know God's wisdom.

390
00:27:15,360 --> 00:27:19,760
Baked within this searching is a desire for God.

391
00:27:19,760 --> 00:27:24,020
They were just looking for it in the wrong places.

392
00:27:24,020 --> 00:27:30,600
They think his power is like strength against their enemies and his wisdom is insight used to improve their earthly status.

393
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:36,860
But Christ crucified shows us that God's power over his enemies is demonstrated through his sacrificial love.

394
00:27:36,860 --> 00:27:43,040
That his wisdom isn't used to elevate his own status, but to elevate the status of those beneath him.

395
00:27:43,040 --> 00:27:47,240
And this is the message that we've been invited to embrace.

396
00:27:47,240 --> 00:27:51,480
It's actually the example that he's called us to follow.

397
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:58,820
And we like to embrace the message without following the example.

398
00:27:58,820 --> 00:28:04,540
Me, first and foremost, in that category.

399
00:28:04,540 --> 00:28:07,360
I love how F.B. Meyer puts it.

400
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:09,560
Such a cool name.

401
00:28:09,560 --> 00:28:16,840
You know, when somebody quotes me like 150 years from now, if one of my sermons ever lives on and somebody quotes me,

402
00:28:16,840 --> 00:28:18,260
and they're like, as Ryan Miller once said.

403
00:28:18,320 --> 00:28:19,340
I'm like, that doesn't sound cool.

404
00:28:19,340 --> 00:28:21,980
F.B. Meyer.

405
00:28:21,980 --> 00:28:25,440
As F.B. Meyer once said, he says,

406
00:28:25,480 --> 00:28:48,360
This is the value of the kingdom of God coming against the value of this world.

407
00:28:49,160 --> 00:28:52,300
That God has actually found as we stoop lower and surrender more.

408
00:28:52,300 --> 00:29:00,740
So we identify the ways in which our idea of wisdom and power come against the ideas of the kingdom.

409
00:29:00,740 --> 00:29:04,320
We examine how this impacts the way that we live our lives.

410
00:29:04,320 --> 00:29:09,520
And ultimately, he wants us to redefine, build our lives on the true values of the kingdom of God.

411
00:29:09,520 --> 00:29:17,900
But to those whom God has called, both Jews and Greeks, Christ is the power of God and the wisdom of God.

412
00:29:17,900 --> 00:29:27,480
The question then becomes for us, do our lives, do our lived values align with the values of the kingdom of God?

413
00:29:29,260 --> 00:29:37,220
Do our lived values, not our intellectually agreed upon values, but do the values that our lives are built on,

414
00:29:37,220 --> 00:29:39,820
do they align with the values of the kingdom of God?

415
00:29:39,820 --> 00:29:45,680
Or are we allowing our cultural values to dominate the way we have received and interacted with the gospel?

416
00:29:45,680 --> 00:29:47,300
This is maturity in the kingdom.

417
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:52,700
Laying down the values of our culture and picking up the values of the kingdom of God.

418
00:29:52,700 --> 00:29:59,400
Even when it looks like foolishness and weakness, it is the power and wisdom of God.

419
00:29:59,400 --> 00:30:07,460
Is the ultimate aim of your life to achieve success by climbing the ladder with influence and wisdom?

420
00:30:07,460 --> 00:30:13,300
Or are we content to trust Christ and meet him at the bottom of the ladder,

421
00:30:13,300 --> 00:30:18,600
trusting that in him we will find abundant and everlasting life?

422
00:30:20,400 --> 00:30:23,400
What is driving our life?

423
00:30:23,400 --> 00:30:27,800
Are we trying to just keep getting a little bit higher, achieve a little bit more success,

424
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:29,660
do a little bit better than our neighbors are doing?

425
00:30:29,660 --> 00:30:37,600
Or are we using our resources and our time and our energy to point to Christ crucified,

426
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:40,760
the power and wisdom of God?

427
00:30:40,760 --> 00:30:47,400
That, I think, in some ways is an easier question to answer than the one I'm going to ask next.

428
00:30:50,400 --> 00:30:55,160
And that is, for those of you that have children, this is where I think it really,

429
00:30:55,160 --> 00:31:00,720
we've really got to work hard to define what it is that we're actually building our lives on,

430
00:31:00,720 --> 00:31:02,660
the values that are actually important to us.

431
00:31:02,660 --> 00:31:04,400
Because it's one thing to ask you,

432
00:31:04,400 --> 00:31:10,400
are you trying to climb the social economic ladder with power and influence and success?

433
00:31:10,400 --> 00:31:13,860
Or are you really trusting in Christ crucified?

434
00:31:13,860 --> 00:31:17,920
It's another thing to ask, what cultural values are you imparting on your kids?

435
00:31:17,920 --> 00:31:25,100
Are we trying to help our kids climb to the top of the social ladder through cultural power and influence?

436
00:31:25,100 --> 00:31:29,620
Are we inviting them to see the beauty of Jesus at the bottom of the worldly ladder?

437
00:31:31,300 --> 00:31:34,580
Are we setting them up for abundant and everlasting life?

438
00:31:34,580 --> 00:31:38,860
Or are we leading them down a path of the anxious generation?

439
00:31:38,860 --> 00:31:40,880
I would just go back to, is it working?

440
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:48,000
Is the way that secular American culture is raising children, is it working?

441
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:53,660
And if it's not working, and if we as objective people can stand back and say, it's not working,

442
00:31:54,220 --> 00:31:58,900
then why is it that we are parenting our children in the exact same way that all of our neighbors are?

443
00:31:58,900 --> 00:32:05,100
Why is it that we are, without words, telling our children that what success looks like

444
00:32:05,100 --> 00:32:09,620
is climbing the ladder of social power and influence is succeeding?

445
00:32:09,620 --> 00:32:12,220
It's not that success is bad.

446
00:32:12,220 --> 00:32:13,520
I'm not saying that.

447
00:32:13,520 --> 00:32:18,560
But what I'm saying is if we build their lives around achieving worldly success,

448
00:32:18,900 --> 00:32:25,680
then what we're inviting them into is to spend their life running a treadmill that's going nowhere.

449
00:32:25,680 --> 00:32:38,180
And maybe I'm just, maybe you guys are suffering the realities of having a pastor who has a two-year-old.

450
00:32:38,180 --> 00:32:40,920
I'm thinking about these things now.

451
00:32:40,920 --> 00:32:43,760
What do I want to give my child?

452
00:32:43,760 --> 00:32:46,680
What values do I want him to see as important in life?

