00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:55,220
So what's interesting to me is Jesus gives us this regular reminder of Christ crucified.

533
00:39:55,220 --> 00:39:57,680
His body broken and his blood shed.

534
00:39:57,680 --> 00:40:04,620
It's, it's, it's almost meant to come in opposition to our cultural values on a regular basis.

535
00:40:05,120 --> 00:40:17,060
It's almost meant to let us look at Christ's body broken, his blood shed on a regular basis because he knows that we are prone to forget.

536
00:40:18,740 --> 00:40:24,520
That the message of the cross looks like weakness and foolishness to the world around us.

537
00:40:24,520 --> 00:40:25,840
And this is what the Corinthians were doing.

538
00:40:25,840 --> 00:40:35,120
They were actually so influenced by their cultural values that even when they were taking his body and his blood, the image of Christ crucified,

539
00:40:35,120 --> 00:40:38,560
they were doing it in a way that promoted power, wealth, and status.

